    "same_direction_propagation_case_present": true,
    "strongest_current_comparative_reading": "Independent island systems repeatedly show common-ish upstream functional or interaction changes followed by multiple downstream states: same-direction propagation in a contemporary access-limited case, branching, buffering/resilience, counterdirectional response, or unresolved adjacent links. The evidence is stronger for state-dependent propagation than for one universal directional island syndrome.",
    "abm_reading": "The declared ABM identifies pre-existing functional trait position as a minimal synthetic generator of within-environment branch sign, while local support and partner effectiveness reallocate branches. Dominica failed the first exact signed-position projection; Hawaii supports signed-position-to-interaction-quality plus reproductive buffering; Ogasawara adds a categorical access-to-reproductive-asymmetry propagation contrast without a numeric signed position.",
    "visual_signal_reading": "Visual signal, including nectar guides, remains an active comparative axis. It is missing in the current Izu and Ogasawara access contracts and is not inferred from floral scent."
